---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="GPA calculator: grade point average from your grades and credits"
  description="Work out your GPA on the 4.0 scale from letter grades and credit hours, subject by subject, and see what a target GPA would take."
>
  <h1>GPA calculator</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Add a row for each subject: the letter grade and the credit hours. The calculator weighs
    each grade by its credits, which is the part people get wrong when they average grades in
    their head.
  </p>
    <figure class="fig fig--school"><img src="/img/gpa.webp" alt="Open books and a notebook on a library desk" width="1200" height="514" decoding="async"></figure>

  <div class="sheet">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Subject (optional)</th><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col" class="num">Credits</th><th scope="col"></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <button class="btn" id="add" type="button">Add a subject</button>
      <button class="btn btn--primary" id="calc" type="button" style="margin-left:0.5rem;">Work out my GPA</button>
    </p>
    <div id="out" aria-live="polite" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <p class="result-note">Your GPA appears here.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How GPA is counted</h2>
  <p>
    Each letter grade carries points: A is 4.0, B is 3.0, C is 2.0, D is 1.0, F is 0. Multiply
    the points by the subject’s credit hours, add those products up, and divide by the total
    credits. A 4 credit B (12 points) pulls the average harder than a 1 credit A (4 points),
    which is exactly the weighting the formula is there to do.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col">Points</th><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col">Points</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>A</td><td class="num">4.0</td><td>C</td><td class="num">2.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A−</td><td class="num">3.7</td><td>C−</td><td class="num">1.7</td></tr>
      <tr><td>B+</td><td class="num">3.3</td><td>D+</td><td class="num">1.3</td></tr>
      <tr><td>B</td><td class="num">3.0</td><td>D</td><td class="num">1.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>B−</td><td class="num">2.7</td><td>D−</td><td class="num">0.7</td></tr>
      <tr><td>C+</td><td class="num">2.3</td><td>F</td><td class="num">0.0</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Colleges vary this table slightly, and some do not use plus and minus at all. If your
    school publishes its own scale, your school’s wins.
  </p>

  <h2>One example, worked by hand</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Subject</th><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col" class="num">Credits</th><th scope="col" class="num">Points × credits</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>History</td><td>A (4.0)</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num">12.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Biology</td><td>B (3.0)</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">12.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>English</td><td>A− (3.7)</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num">11.1</td></tr>
      <tr class="point"><td>Total</td><td>35.1 ÷ 10 credits</td><td class="num">10</td><td class="num">GPA 3.51</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Questions people ask</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>What is a good GPA?</dt>
    <dd>
      3.0 is a B average and the line many employers and graduate programmes ask for. 3.5 and
      above is strong at most colleges. Context matters: a 3.3 in a hard engineering programme
      with heavy credit loads is not the same achievement as a 3.3 somewhere lighter, and
      admissions tutors know it.
    </dd>
    <dt>How much can one semester move my GPA?</dt>
    <dd>
      Less each year, because the denominator grows. To hit a target: the average you need in
      what is left is (target × total credits when finished − points already earned) ÷ credits
      still to take. If that number comes out above 4.0, the target is out of reach this term,
      and knowing that early is worth more than hoping.
    </dd>
    <dt>Does this work outside the United States?</dt>
    <dd>
      The 4.0 scale is American. France marks out of 20 and averages with coefficients, Spain
      out of 10, Britain uses degree classes. The French and Spanish versions of this page use
      those systems instead of converting, because a converted grade is not a real grade
      anywhere.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="meta">Method: grade points weighted by credit hours, standard US 4.0 scale. Page last checked 13 November 2026.</p>

  <script>
    const rowsEl = document.getElementById('rows');
    const out = document.getElementById('out');
    const GRADES = ['A', 'A-', 'B+', 'B', 'B-', 'C+', 'C', 'C-', 'D+', 'D', 'D-', 'F'];
    const POINTS = { 'A': 4.0, 'A-': 3.7, 'B+': 3.3, 'B': 3.0, 'B-': 2.7, 'C+': 2.3, 'C': 2.0, 'C-': 1.7, 'D+': 1.3, 'D': 1.0, 'D-': 0.7, 'F': 0.0 };

    function addRow(name, grade, credits) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const opts = GRADES.map((g) => '<option' + (g === grade ? ' selected' : '') + '>' + g + '</option>').join('');
      tr.innerHTML =
        '<td><input type="text" class="g-name" value="' + (name || '') + '" aria-label="Subject name" /></td>' +
        '<td><select class="g-grade" aria-label="Grade">' + opts + '</select></td>' +
        '<td><input type="number" class="g-credits" value="' + (credits || 3) + '" min="0" step="0.5" aria-label="Credits" /></td>' +
        '<td><button type="button" class="btn g-del">Remove</button></td>';
      tr.querySelector('.g-del').addEventListener('click', () => { tr.remove(); });
      rowsEl.appendChild(tr);
    }

    addRow('History', 'A', 3);
    addRow('Biology', 'B', 4);
    addRow('English', 'A-', 3);

    document.getElementById('add').addEventListener('click', () => addRow('', 'A', 3));

    document.getElementById('calc').addEventListener('click', () => {
      let pts = 0;
      let crs = 0;
      rowsEl.querySelectorAll('tr').forEach((tr) => {
        const g = tr.querySelector('.g-grade').value;
        const c = parseFloat(tr.querySelector('.g-credits').value) || 0;
        pts += POINTS[g] * c;
        crs += c;
      });
      if (!crs) {
        out.innerHTML = '<p class="result-note">Add at least one subject with credits and your GPA appears here.</p>';
        return;
      }
      out.innerHTML =
        '<p class="result-figure">GPA ' + (pts / crs).toFixed(2) + '</p>' +
        '<p>That is ' + pts.toFixed(1) + ' grade points across ' + crs + ' credits. Every credit at an A adds 4 points to the top line, which is why heavy subjects move the number most.</p>';
    });
  </script>
</Base>
